            <ArticleTitle>Kinetic Benchmarking Reveals the Competence of Prenyl Groups in Ring-Closing Metathesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5332-5335</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02492</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of prenyl-containing malonates are kinetically benchmarked against the standard allyl-containing congeners using a ruthenium benzylidene precatalyst for ring-closing metatheses. The prenyl grouping is found to be a superior acceptor olefin compared to an allyl group in RCM processes with ruthenium alkylidenes derived from terminal alkenes. The prenyl group is also found to be a highly competent acceptor for a ruthenium alkylidene derived from a 1,1-disubstituted olefin in a RCM process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
